CORE
legacy.c
--unwind 10 --unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
On Windows, _vsnprintf (the Universal CRT's __stdio_common_vsprintf without
_CRT_INTERNAL_PRINTF_STANDARD_SNPRINTF_BEHAVIOR) writes up to the buffer's size
characters and null-terminates them only if there is room; an output longer than
the buffer gives -1, except for the size query _vsnprintf(NULL, 0, ...).
Elsewhere this test is vacuous.
